      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "BTK is a promising target for the treatment of multiple diseases such as B cell malignances, asthma, and rheumatoid arthritis. Here, we report the discovery of a series of novel pyrimidine analogs as potent, highly selective, non-covalent inhibitors of BTK. Compound 25d demonstrated higher affinity to an unactivated conformation of BTK that resulted in an excellent kinase selectivity. Compound 25d showed a good oral bioavailability in mice, and significantly inhibits the PCA reaction in mice."
      },
